# NOTE: engine-strict is deliberately NOT enabled.
#
# package.json declares engines.node "20.x" to match the Dockerfile (node:20-bullseye)
# and CI. Turning on engine-strict would make npm REFUSE to install on any other
# version — correct in principle, but it hard-blocks a machine running Node 22 until
# it downgrades, and that should be a decision, not a surprise from a config file.
#
# The drift is surfaced instead by: .nvmrc (nvm/fnm auto-switch), the engines warning
# npm prints on install, and the pre-push hook which checks the major version.
